[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475695171","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2475695171","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2475695171,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TkBxD","user":{"login":"fire","id":32321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T08:20:37Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T08:21:01Z","body":"What is the benefit of deleting old gcc 8 versions? RHEL8, Alma Linux 8 and Rocky 8 still use gcc 8. \r\n\r\n>  RHEL8 : gcc 8.x or gcc 9.x in app stream.\r\n\r\nhttps://access.redhat.com/solutions/19458","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475695171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475700157","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2475700157","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2475700157,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TkC-9","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-14T08:23:23Z","updated_at":"2024-11-14T08:23:37Z","body":"> What is the benefit of deleting old gcc 8 versions? RHEL8, Alma Linux 8 and Rocky 8 still use gcc 8.\r\n> \r\n> > RHEL8 : gcc 8.x or gcc 9.x in app stream.\r\n> \r\n> https://access.redhat.com/solutions/19458\r\n\r\nWe already require minimum gcc 9:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/76fa7b291455a8ba24c50005072ebdb58f8a5984/SConstruct#L642-L650\r\n\r\nSo having a check if compiler is < 8 doesn't have any sense","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2475700157/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478484120","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2478484120","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2478484120,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TuqqY","user":{"login":"shana","id":310137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDEzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/310137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana","html_url":"https://github.com/shana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T10:16:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T10:16:27Z","body":"> Looks good to me.\r\n> \r\n> The only risk is if the `is_apple_clang` method is not 100% reliable, it might then wrongly flag actual Apple clang builds as not Apple (other false negatives wouldn't be a problem). So this needs to be tested on macOS and with osxcross cross-compilation on Linux just to be sure.\r\n\r\nThis could also affect console platforms that use clang toolchains and could be misidentified. I would lean towards being a bit more paranoid about using both `is_apple_clang` and other more specific platform checks to make sure only apple platforms really fall into that condition.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478484120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478532289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2478532289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2478532289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tu2bB","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T10:42:43Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T10:43:30Z","body":"> > Looks good to me.\r\n> > The only risk is if the `is_apple_clang` method is not 100% reliable, it might then wrongly flag actual Apple clang builds as not Apple (other false negatives wouldn't be a problem). So this needs to be tested on macOS and with osxcross cross-compilation on Linux just to be sure.\r\n> \r\n> This could also affect console platforms that use clang toolchains and could be misidentified. I would lean towards being a bit more paranoid about using both `is_apple_clang` and other more specific platform checks to make sure only apple platforms really fall into that condition.\r\n\r\nI think the risk is when using Xcode actually, because if anything goes wrong, `is_apple_clang` can only return `False`. I don't see a case where it would return a false positive (`True`), the only way for it to be `True` is if the version string starts with `Apple`.\r\n\r\nIf it returns `False` while using Xcode, then yeah it might use the wrong branches. But that would imply that the current code only works by chance - I just want it tested to confirm but I don't think it's actually broken :P\r\n\r\nSo other platforms shouldn't be affected.\r\n\r\nBTW I just tested with osxcross, and it doesn't identify itself as \"AppleClang\", and its version string is the one of vanilla LLVM (despite me building the Apple fork of Clang), so it seems like this is really for Xcode's weird versioning that we need the `apple_clang` stuff.\r\n```\r\n$ clang --version\r\nclang version 16.0.0 (https://github.com/tpoechtrager/osxcross ff8d100f3f026b4ffbe4ce96d8aac4ce06f1278b)\r\n```\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThat being said, while probably unnecessary, I see no harm in adding a platform check in `is_apple_clang` for extra safety.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478532289/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478567963","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2478567963","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2478567963,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tu_Ib","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T11:02:32Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T11:02:32Z","body":"I just curious about why `is_vanilla_clang` which is just negative twin of `is_apple_clang` wasn't questionable?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478567963/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478605720","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2478605720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2478605720,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TvIWY","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T11:25:00Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T11:25:00Z","body":"> I just curious about why `is_vanilla_clang` which is just negative twin of `is_apple_clang` wasn't questionable?\r\n\r\nIt is, but since it was only used for macOS/iOS, and it's in support of a very niche use case (far most users building for macOS/iOS do it with Xcode on macOS which isn't vanilla LLVM/Clang), it wasn't as problematic if it's misidentified.\r\n\r\nWhen flipping the meaning to cover what is the expected toolchain for 99% of use cases, we need to make sure it's reliable.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2478605720/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479415049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99217#issuecomment-2479415049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99217","id":2479415049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TyN8J","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T16:47:09Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T16:47:09Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479415049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]